+## Routes
+
+- `POST /import/sales`: body `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }`.
+  Each row sells a positive whole number of recipe portions. `soldAt` is an
+  ISO instant with a timezone; consumption is recorded at that instant with
+  `ref` `sale:<ticket>`. Returns `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`, counting
+  new tickets and total portions sold. Previously imported tickets are skipped.
+  Every row is validated; an invalid row or shortage rejects the whole file
+  with a `bad_request` error naming its row (the first data row is row 2).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`: inclusive UTC days;
+  `from` must be on or before `to`. Returns an array of
+  `{ "itemId": 1, "theoretical": 2, "actual": 3, "difference": 1 }`.
+  Difference is actual minus theoretical. Actual includes every `consume`
+  movement; theoretical uses ingredient quantities saved with each sale.
+  Only items with positive theoretical or actual use appear, in item id order.
