+## Sales (schema 3)
+
+- Schema 2 files migrate by adding an empty `sales` collection and a `sale`
+  sequence. Each sale has an id, ticket, soldAt (normalized UTC instant),
+  dishId, qty, and an `ingredients` snapshot of scaled itemId/qty pairs.
+- A ticket is imported once, including all its rows in that file. An import
+  commits its sales, batch changes, movements and sequences together.
+- Sales consume stock at soldAt with ledger ref `sale:<ticket>`. Variance
+  uses saved ingredients so later recipe changes do not rewrite history.
